<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίδῐμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			4.28
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>N.</u>
			1.68
		</span></i> (not used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> in fem.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαιδρός</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shining, radiant,
			glistening,</i> esp. of men's limbs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ὦμος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.128
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				1.27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.27
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				492
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					1.68
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσοψις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.28
				</span></i>
			 (s. v. l.); <i>sleek, glossy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>O.</u>
					6.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of heroes,
				<i>famous, glorious,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίδιμ᾽ Ἀχιλλεῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.434
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίδιμ᾽ Ὀδυσσεῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.251
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίδιμος Ἕκτωρ, αἴας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.505
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.617
			</span></i>, etc.—Used by Trag. only in 
				Ep.
			 phrases, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαίδιμ᾽ Ἀχιλλεῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					131
				</span></i>
			 (anap., ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				992
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφὶ φ. ὤμοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					453
				</span></i>
			; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. βραχίονες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Achae.
					4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
